{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792348767,"nonce":"bMtoW+FOPT4oU0yLt3i1OtLs4n8=","message":"Decisions from the user, 2026-10-18:\n- An extension project is opened from its own config file, a .rayext (JSON), as a Haxe project is from a .hxml. No build.hxml, no compilation server. It replaces extension.json from the draft plan (971d58e): the same fields (name, version, description, main, capabilities, contributes) plus sources, mocks and a view. The Settings list of installed extensions reads .rayext files.\n- It is also edited from a form in RayDE, not only as text.\n- The extension's view has a custom icon (an SVG file the config names), a title, and a location: it picks which part of the layout the view is drawn in. By default it is the sidebar: its icon is added to the activity bar and swaps with the Explorer. Other locations: the right side bar, a bottom panel tab, an editor tab.\n- So the Studio shows the extension where it will really be, not only in a pane beside the code. The Studio's controls (reload, live, mocks, state) are a header on the view while it is in development. A .rays file outside a .rayext project keeps the preview beside its code.\n- Unsaved edits to the extension's other scripts are sent to the host, so a live reload runs what is in the editor.\nConfig shape: {name, version, description, main, sources, mocks, capabilities, view: {title, icon, location}}.","files":null}]}